        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img alt="" loading="lazy" id="w-node-_2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63771-83c22e73" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6928117b581ddc6a7e8b90dd_Metadata%20Injection%20cover%20(2).png" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6928117b581ddc6a7e8b90dd_Metadata%20Injection%20cover%20(2)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6928117b581ddc6a7e8b90dd_Metadata%20Injection%20cover%20(2)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6928117b581ddc6a7e8b90dd_Metadata%20Injection%20cover%20(2)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/6928117b581ddc6a7e8b90dd_Metadata%20Injection%20cover%20(2).png 1200w" class="post-image"><div class="post-content-div"><div class="div-block-992"><div class="div-block-1010"><div fs-list-field="category" class="blog-category">Cloud Detection &amp; Response </div><div class="highlight-tag pop">Popular</div><div class="highlight-tag w-condition-invisible">Highlights</div><div class="hide w-dyn-list"><div role="list" class="w-dyn-items"><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">CDR</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">GitHub</div></div><div role="listitem" class="w-dyn-item"><div fs-list-field="Topic">Kubernetes</div></div></div></div></div><a data-wf-native-id-path="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775_instance-0" data-wf-ao-click-engagement-tracking="true" data-wf-element-id="2e7022be-dae3-cc3c-2a30-63bd4fd63775" data-wf-cms-context="%5B%7B%22collectionId%22%3A%2265dbcab8c88303f083c22dc7%22%2C%22itemId%22%3A%22692809de95f899009634a2b0%22%7D%5D" href="/post/the-shai-hulud-2-0-npm-worm-what-happened-how-stream-detected-it" class="b-title w-inline-block"><h2 fs-list-field="title" class="heading-29 blog">The Shai-Hulud 2.0 npm Worm: What Happened &amp; How Stream Detected It</h2><div class="blog-par limit-char">Shai-Hulud 2.0 is rapidly backdooring npm packages, spawning tens of thousands of malicious repos, and stealing developer creds. In this blog, we detonate an infected package and show how Stream Security instantly detects and investigates the threat with behavioral analytics + AI Triage (with real Stream platform images included). </div></a></div><div class="divider-full space small"></div><div class="div-block-773"><div class="writer-small dark"><img height="70" width="70" alt="Petr Zuzanov" src="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png" sizes="70px" srcset="https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-500.png 500w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-800.png 800w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23)-p-1080.png 1080w, https://cdn.prod.website-files.com/5f05d5858fab461d0d08eaeb/68adfa06ebf00dbc01e2501c_image%20(23).png 1400w" class="writer-image-small"><div><div fs-list-field="author" class="writer---blog-page-home">Petr Zuzanov</div></div></div><div class="div-block-790 xs"><div class="div-block-953"><div class="writer---blog-page-home date">Nov 27, 2025</div></div><div class="code-embed-3 w-embed"><svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
